      "title": "Australia news live: new Labor president Kate Ellis warns party against ‘turning hurt into anger’; Hanson accuses media of twisting her words on DV",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/23/australia-news-live-china-penny-wong-asean-labor-conference-anthony-albanese-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Treasurer says ‘parties of the sensible centre and the centre-left parties’ face ‘serious economic challenges’. Follow live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Self-reported domestic violence incidents declining in NSW but deaths and hospitalisations fail to fall</strong></p><p>New data shows self-reported domestic violence incidents in New South Wales have declined, but the number of women and children murdered or hospitalised in domestic and family violence incidents over the past eight years has not significantly budged.</p><p>The decline in self-reported violence is significant because it reflects underlying levels of violence in the community, not just what is reported to police. It suggests that, despite rising reports of domestic violence to police, domestic violence in the community is not increasing and may be trending down.</p><p>There’s a strong perception that violence against women is rising, which is understandable given increases in police-recorded incidents, heightened media attention and greater public awareness.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/23/australia-news-live-china-penny-wong-asean-labor-conference-anthony-albanese-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-23T01:28:52"
    },
    {
      "title": "AusAlert test will blast emergency warning siren over most phones in Australia on Monday. Here’s what to know",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/22/ausalert-test-sound-national-alert-emergency-warning-system-date",
      "description": "<p>National emergency test alert will be sent to all mobile devices on 27 July, with domestic violence advocates advising how to turn off safe phones</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/23/australia-news-live-china-penny-wong-asean-labor-conference-anthony-albanese-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Virtually every phone in the country will blare an emergency siren at 2pm AEST on Monday 27 July as part of the first Australia-wide test of a new national warning system called AusAlert.</p><p>Most phones, and some smartwatches and tablets, will receive a pop-up notification and an alert sound that cannot be silenced – even if your device is on “do not disturb” or silent mode.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/22/ausalert-test-sound-national-alert-emergency-warning-system-date\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-22T15:00:20"
    },
    {
      "title": "How will Australia’s emergency services cope if satellites go down? With a sextant and a street directory",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/23/australia-emergency-services-satellites-down",
      "description": "<p>Military and SES personnel being taught analog communication and navigation techniques as experts warn solar flare could knock out ‘critical space infrastructure’</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/23/australia-news-live-china-penny-wong-asean-labor-conference-anthony-albanese-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Australia’s emergency services and military personnel are being trained to read paper maps, navigate without GPS support and sail by the stars in case something knocks out the nation’s space capabilities.</p><p>A panel at the 19th Australian Space Forum in Adelaide on Wednesday was asked to consider what would happen “if we suddenly lost access to critical space infrastructure – no satellites, no GPS, no remote sensing, no secure communications?”</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/23/australia-emergency-services-satellites-down\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-22T15:00:19"
    },
    {
      "title": "Why are OpenAI and Anthropic cheering on regulation in Australia? The answer has global reach",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/23/openai-anthropic-australia-ai-regulation",
      "description": "<p>The companies hope to follow in the footsteps of SpaceX, which raised $86bn and soared to a $2.1tn valuation after it listed on public markets in June</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Top US AI developers Anthropic and OpenAI cheered when Australia announced it would set new AI rules.</p><p>Big tech celebrating limits on their Silicon Valley VC-funded free-for-all might seem counterintuitive but there’s a much broader play than just what happens in one relatively small market.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jul/23/openai-anthropic-australia-ai-regulation\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-22T15:00:19"
    },
    {
      "title": "Great Barrier Reef microbiome mapped as researchers discover 500 bacterial species previously unknown to science",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/23/great-barrier-reef-microbiome-mapped-as-researchers-discover-500-bacterial-species-previously-unknown-to-science",
      "description": "<p>Research identifies 808,585 viral genomes belonging to what scientists estimate to be 362,802 different viruses</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/23/australia-news-live-china-penny-wong-asean-labor-conference-anthony-albanese-one-nation-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>More than a decade after the <a href=\"https://www.nature.com/articles/nature11234\">human microbiome</a> was comprehensively mapped, scientists have now identified the vast communities of microbes that make up the Great Barrier Reef.</p><p>Analysing DNA from seawater samples of 48 reefs, researchers have mapped the microbiome of the Great Barrier Reef, documenting more than 360,000 distinct viruses as well as more than 500 new bacterial species not previously known to science.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/jul/23/great-barrier-reef-microbiome-mapped-as-researchers-discover-500-bacterial-species-previously-unknown-to-science\">Continue reading...</a>",
